dom and  constitutionality and whatever  dealing with the virus most quickly  will help the economy and we have  examples of it new zealand did an  incredible job dealing with the virus  they didn't need long debates over  whether to open or close or max or not  they just they did it they dealt with it  and then they had long periods of  normality where much of the rest of the  world  was very far from normality israel in  terms of vaccination israel was  able to strike a deal early with pfizer  uh being a country of only nine million  people to get enough doses for everybody  uh in exchange for sharing data with  pfizer  uh businesses are open in israel  passover was almost completely normal in  israel  a couple of weeks ago the entire time  the united states wasted time with  conversations that were being forced  upon us  by the right by the trumpists by the  anti-massacres by whoever else  and all along the best medical policy  was the best economic policy that's what  we learned and it is increasingly  borne out in the data that we get had we  figured out testing earlier instead of  trump saying  we don't need this slow down testing 15  cases will go to zero if we just figured  out testing and were able  to contain it we would have had a  problem of course we would have had a  problem in a country of 330 million  people  but it wouldn't have gotten as bad as it  did the economy would have gotten better  more quickly  had we had competent leadership early  the economy would have done better  all along other good indicators uh  economically by the way retail sales  up uh about nine percent higher in march  that is uh significant a lot of it is  coming from bars and restaurants  and other uh business areas um  and then the result of all of this is  the stock market popping today  all-time highs you're not seeing joe  biden tweet endlessly about it  but the dow jones industrial average was  up more than 200 points  as of when i looked at it half an hour  ago um  hit an all-time high the s p 500 hitting  an intraday  record like forever the the forever  record was hit today  uh nasdaq up one percent of course the  economy is not the stock market  but the point is all of it together  confirms  that the better we do against the virus  that's the economic policy  it's not the debate between public  health policy  and economic policy it's all the same  the economy does better when we better  deal with the virus  we better deal with the virus when we  understand  that we don't need to think about the  virus as separate and distinct from the  economy  because it all goes hand in hand we'll  hope for continued  improvement in the numbers my belief is  and again i always make very clear i'm  not  coming up with this stuff on my own i'm  looking at the public health experts  because they are the experts  it seems as though 40 days from now  numbers will look significantly better  and hopefully as a result economic  numbers will as well  one of our sponsors is vincero watches  giving you 15  off a high quality wristwatch is the  perfect way to  elevate your style own at least one  watch  that makes you feel great when you put  it on you can often see me wearing  my ventura watch on the show mine is the  gunmetal  vessel model i'm a big fan of the  metallic look  of the face of the watch i like the  silicone strap  you won't find a better made watch for  this good a price  anywhere else when you put it on you  know you got more than you paid for  vincero believes in crafting super  quality watches from high-end materials  but selling them at  fair prices which is why they have over  twenty six thousand  five star reviews and they stand behind  every watch they make with a one-year  return policy  and five-year warranty they'll give you  fifteen percent off everything in their  store and free shipping  at davidpakman.com watch use the coupon  code  pacman
 

